          "upstreamBehaviour": "multi-line inserted values keep column-0 layout after the first line, so nested members sit one level too shallow",
          "labBehaviour": "every line after the first is prefixed with the insertion indent, aligning the nested value with its siblings",
          "reason": "upstream-bug: modify('{\\n  \"a\": 1\\n}', ['b'], {c:{d:1}}) applies upstream with the nested object mis-indented; upstream tests only assert include('\\t\"b\"')"
