          "labBehaviour": "JsoncEdit.applyAll throws the tagged JsoncEditOverlapError {lower, upper}; JsoncEdit.applyAllResult returns it as a Result failure",
          "reason": "law:7 (no native Error in production source; extend S.TaggedError)"
        },
        {
          "test": "scratchpad/test/jsonc/JsoncModifier.test.ts:55 and scratchpad/test/jsonc/Properties.test.ts (JsoncModifier insert property)",
          "upstreamBehaviour": "with a trailing comma before the closer, navigate scans past the closer and inserts outside the container: modify('{ \"a\": 1, }', ['delta'], []) yields '{ \"a\": 1, },\\n  \"delta\": []' (unparseable); '{ \"a\": { \"b\": 1, } }' at ['a','c'] writes c into the parent; '[1, ]' at [1] yields '[1, ,\\n  2]'",
          "labBehaviour": "a comma followed by the closer ends the scan, so the insertion lands after the last member inside the container and the result parses to the expected value",
          "reason": "upstream-bug: the default JSONC options accept trailing commas, and the property 'JsoncModifier insert' (result parses to {...doc, delta: next}) fails upstream on '{ \"a\": 1, }'; upstream tests never insert into a trailing-comma container"
        }
